2. Algorithm
Start the program.
Define a class named Stud.
Accept marks of five subjects from the user.
Calculate the total and average marks.
Define a method to display the total and average.
Define another method to calculate the grade based on the average.
Create an object of the class.
Call the methods using the object.
Display the output.
Stop the program.


class op:
    x = int(input("enter the value of x:"))
    y = int(input("enter the value of y:"))

    def add(self):
        print("addition: ", self.x + self.y)

    def sub(self):
        print("subtraction: ", self.x - self.y)

    def mul(self):
        print("multiplication: ", self.x * self.y)

    def div(self):
        print("division: ", self.x / self.y)

    def mod(self):
        print("modulus: ", self.x % self.y)


s = op()
s.add()
s.sub()
s.mul()
s.div()
s.mod()

